&lt;b&gt;POS-34054&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Revenue Accounting (Operations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Manager, Revenue Accounting to run the execution side of our revenue accounting function. You will own the monthly and quarterly revenue close, the revenue sub-ledger and reconciliations, and the control environment around them, and you will drive automation so the close scales with the business. You will partner closely with the Senior Manager, Technical Revenue Accounting, who sets the technical conclusions, while you make sure they are applied accurately and on time in the system and the close. The company&#39;s pricing and consumption models are evolving and you will need to keep the close process, system configuration, and controls aligned as those changes occur.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you&#39;ll get to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the revenue close, including the close calendar, sub-ledger reconciliations, contract asset and receivable roll-forwards, and revenue journal entries and flux analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of revenue accountants, setting priorities, reviewing work, and building a culture of accuracy and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day operation of the revenue system and its integrations (e.g., AREV, NetSuite, Looker), including rule configuration, and data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply policies and conclusions from Technical Revenue Accounting in routine contract reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the revenue SOX control environment, including control design and operation, evidence, remediation, and audit walkthroughs and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review revenue disclosures for quarterly SEC reporting, including RPO, revenue by location, and deferred revenue roll-forwards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely revenue reporting to FP&amp;amp;A and support forecasting and bookings-to-revenue bridges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvement and automation, using AI tools and workflow technology to reduce manual effort in reconciliations, variance analysis, and close, with controls in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize new pricing, packaging, launches, and evolving consumption models by translating accounting guidance into system configuration, data requirements, and close procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are looking for people who have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive professional accounting experience, including leading teams, in a public company SaaS or technology environment and/or a Big 4 or national firm; CPA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of ASC 606 and the ability to apply established policy to a high volume of contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience owning a month-end and quarter-end revenue close in a public company, with a record of improving cycle time and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with revenue reporting infrastructure (e.g., AREV, NetSuite, or similar), including sub-ledger reconciliation and system implementation or enhancement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of SOX compliance, internal controls, and audit support, and SEC reporting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A process-minded, data-driven approach, with advanced Excel and SQL or BI skills a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, prioritization, and stakeholder management skills across Accounting, Finance Systems, Billing, Sales Ops, and FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, with the ability to explain close status, variances, and risks to senior finance leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with change: able to adjust close processes, system configuration, and controls quickly as pricing and consumption models evolve, while keeping the close on schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
