&lt;b&gt;POS-34053&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Technical Revenue Accounting (Individual Contributor)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Manager, Technical Revenue Accounting to be the company&#39;s deepest ASC 606 technical resource below the Director of Revenue. You will research and conclude on complex and non-standard revenue arrangements, shape revenue policy, and make sure new pricing, packaging, and go-to-market initiatives are accounted for correctly and on time. The company&#39;s pricing and consumption models are evolving quickly as the business moves deeper into AI, and revenue accounting has to move with it. This role needs someone who adapts quickly, is comfortable with ambiguity, and can reach sound accounting conclusions while the business model is evolving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you&#39;ll get to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical accounting conclusions for complex and non-standard contracts, including multi-element arrangements, variable consideration, customer incentives, contract modifications, and usage-based and consumption pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and maintain global ASC 606 policy, technical memos, and position papers that evolve with the business and stand up to auditor and SEC scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review contract waterfalls and calculations for complex arrangements, including material rights and termination provisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the stand-alone selling price (SSP) determination and refresh process, including supporting documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage early in go-to-market initiatives, such as pricing changes, launches, bundling, and evolving consumption models, to separate accounting requirements from business choices, flag risks before terms are final, and recommend practical alternatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Deal Desk, Product, Pricing, Legal, and FP&amp;amp;A on non-standard contract structures and approval frameworks, explaining accounting implications in plain language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain SOX controls over contract review, SSP, and other judgment-based processes, and support walkthroughs and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define accounting requirements for new revenue scenarios in the revenue system ( AREV) and work with Revenue Operations, Finance Systems, and the Senior Manager, Revenue Accounting to test and validate configuration changes and system assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach revenue accountants and partner teams on technical topics and the principles behind policies and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead special projects and company-wide initiatives that need deep technical revenue expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to speed up research, contract review, and memo drafting, with appropriate review and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are looking for people who have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive accounting experience with a focus on technical revenue accounting, including public accounting (Big 4 or national firm) and a public company SaaS or technology environment; CPA required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of ASC 606 and US GAAP, especially for SaaS, usage-based, and multi-product bundled revenue models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of writing technical accounting memos and defending conclusions with external auditors and the SEC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing internal controls based on a thorough grasp of the fact pattern and the risks, with strong knowledge of SOX compliance and SEC reporting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of revenue systems (e.g., AREV, NetSuite, Oracle RMCS, Zuora Revenue, or similar) and the ability to translate technical accounting into system requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain complex accounting impacts to executives and non-accountants at the right level of detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment: able to cut through the noise to the core of a problem, take a position, document the reasoning, and hold it under challenge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and influence working relationships at all levels across Sales, Product, Legal, and Finance without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of adapting quickly in a changing business: comfortable with ambiguity, able to reset priorities on short notice, and able to reach defensible conclusions on evolving pricing and consumption models before precedent exists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
